{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014uBqP9DPvR53THP8qrrXAD","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/7e0f410179f755c7f1d64e80833584d3460c746dcb3ad83e944d3be87642747d.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task usb4stream-bench: Author the wedge-safe stream-primitive first-light bench, its receipts bound, and the transport decision memo. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"bench/usb4stream-bench.py\\\",\\\"docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md\\\",\\\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:8b10c85320a9b74be4924db88ce4730ec43ac641c1ec58463ffee983b807dbce\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"python3 -m py_compile bench/usb4stream-bench.py scripts/receipts-verify.py && grep -q 'configfs' bench/usb4stream-bench.py && grep -q 'usb4stream' scripts/receipts-verify.py && ! grep -qE '/dev/tbstream[0-9]' bench/usb4stream-bench.py && grep -q 'serve-up-on-shared-cable' bench/usb4stream-bench.py && test -s docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md && python3 -m unittest tests.test_usb4stream_bench -v\"],\"description\":\"Bench and checker compile, resolution is configfs-driven with no hardcoded device node, the serve-up skip exists, the memo exists, and the tests pass.\",\"id\":\"usb4stream-bench-sound\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"bench/usb4stream-bench.py\",\"docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md\",\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"A single-open, skip-safe, retry-proof bench that can bank the first stream-primitive exchange numbers without being able to storm the hop tables, and that refuses to touch the device while the pair is serving on the same cable\",\"The morning reads one memo that settles plugin-versus-port with trigger criteria instead of re-deliberating\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Author (never run — the dead-last checkpoint runs it) a wedge-safe first-light benchmark of the in-tree USB4 stream primitive, as transport-decision evidence for the morning. Deliverables: (1) bench/usb4stream-bench.py — one file serving both roles (coordinator role is the default; peer role via --role peer --dev PATH; the peer is launched by streaming this same file over the control wire: ssh worker with the script on stdin, never a copy). Non-negotiable mechanics, each existing because an open/close storm against a mismatched peer wedges router hop tables and already darkened rail 0 once: (a) NEVER hardcode a numbered device node and never write a digit directly after the word tbstream anywhere in the file — the numbering is asymmetric across the twins and the coordinator carries PEERLESS cable-B groups at the low indices, where a blocking open waits forever; resolve on EACH node as: the rail netdev carrying the 10.99.0.0/30 address, then readlink /sys/class/net/RAIL/device, then the parent xdomain, then the sibling service whose key attribute is stream, then the configfs group fn0's index attribute, then the device node /dev/tbstream suffixed with that index; require BOTH ends' fn0 configfs groups to exist before any open. (b) Exactly ONE open attempt per side, ever, blocking, under a 30 s alarm; any failure after that point: close whatever is open, kill the ssh child, write the receipt, exit — never reopen, never retry, never write configfs (read ring_size and throttling only). (c) Idempotence guard: if results/receipts/usb4stream.json already exists, exit 0 immediately WITHOUT touching any device — this is what makes harness retries storm-free by construction. (d) Skip preconditions, checked in this order BEFORE any device access, each producing receipt status pass with data.outcome 'skipped:REASON' and exit 0: (i) the pair serve is up — the API answers on the coordinator, or podman reports the serving container running on either node (check the worker over the control wire) — outcome 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable': the stream device shares cable A with the serving rails and a wedge would take the campaign's headline deliverable down, so this bench runs ONLY on an idle cable; (ii) ping -c1 -W2 to the rail peer fails — outcome 'skipped:rail-peer-unreachable'; (iii) either end's fn0 configfs group is missing — outcome 'skipped:configfs-group-missing'. Record data.serve_up true or false in EVERY receipt including skips. (e) Fixed schedule, no adaptivity, no retries: 50 iterations of 4 KiB ping-pong warmup (discarded); RTT at 64, 4096, 16384, 65536 bytes times 500 iterations with p50 and p99 per size; the allreduce-shaped simultaneous exchange at 8192, 16384, 65536 bytes times 500 (both sides write N bytes then read N bytes — ring 1024 times 4 KiB frames buffers this safely); throughput 256 MiB each direction; under 90 s wall total, whole run under a global timeout. (f) The receipt at results/receipts/usb4stream.json: one JSON object, step 'usb4stream', status ALWAYS 'pass' — this bench is evidence-gathering, not a campaign claim, so a mid-run abort is typed as data.outcome 'aborted:PHASE:ERRNO' rather than a fail status that would redden every later gate run; data carries outcome, per-size rtt and exchange p50/p99 fields, throughput both directions, ring_size and throttling as read from configfs, resolved device paths on both ends, open_count (assert exactly 1 per side), serve_up, and loop 'python' for honesty about syscall-loop overhead. (2) scripts/receipts-verify.py: add a 'usb4stream' entry to the BOUNDS table — outcome 'ok' requires open_count 1 and all schedule fields present; 'skipped:' and 'aborted:' outcomes require their reason text and pass. (3) docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md — the decision memo: why the collective-library net-plugin route is REJECTED for the latency goal (it sits under the library's proxy and protocol stack, HopID scarcity shared with the network paths forces a multiplexer over one or two long-lived streams, and comm teardown on every serve restart is exactly the open/close pattern the wedge hazard forbids; 3-5 attended days to a fragile prototype, 2-4 attended weeks to overnight-trustworthy); why the real path is a 2-4 attended-day port of the reference doorbell-plus-progress-thread allreduce (the 105 microsecond reference bar) from verbs onto the stream device's read and write, with the receive path run by the progress thread; the morning trigger criteria (banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix showing allreduce-dominated decode); the note that after a healthy night the first real run happens attended in the morning AFTER the pair is torn down (the serve-up skip is deliberate); and a drafted-not-filed issue body for the port. (4) tests/test_usb4stream_bench.py: py-compile both edited python files, assert the no-hardcoded-device-node invariant (no digit after tbstream in the bench source), assert the idempotence guard and the serve-up skip are present, and exercise the receipts checker's three outcome branches with synthetic receipt dicts. Boundaries: touch only bench/usb4stream-bench.py, docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md, scripts/receipts-verify.py, and tests/.\",\"id\":\"usb4stream-bench\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\",\"bench/run-matrix.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:75b32ae929f161f972eb9544f33d653ee19a939a595012f6c112e3c4e69bb00e\",\"title\":\"Author the wedge-safe stream-primitive first-light bench, its receipts bound, and the transport decision memo\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"0a89657f40b8654fed9a050b77458f46f0e5c559\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-ddeb5a9a4133/usb4stream-bench\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"bench/usb4stream-bench.py\",\"docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md\",\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/usb4stream-bench-75b32ae929f161f9\",\"taskId\":\"usb4stream-bench\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ddeb5a9a4133/usb4stream-bench\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE (all tasks — harness limitation, tally#622 family): the spec-build driver fails any lane whose squash merge stages ZERO change against the witnessed base (\\\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\\\", exit 1), even when your no-change conclusion is technically correct. If you verify your deliverables are already fully present and acceptance passes, you must STILL land one small non-empty commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your task's ownership paths: a short RECONCILE-<taskId>-2026-08-30.md note recording HEAD at verification and the acceptance evidence. Never conclude \\\"no commit needed\\\"; never use --allow-empty (squash still stages nothing). This applies especially to checkpoint re-runs whose outputs match the previously committed state byte-for-byte.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/2\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[2],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":0,\"recheckedCursor\":2,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dad2f56-3033-4a9b-8df9-7c3428d04797","uuid":"ac8038d2-b92f-4826-a075-7e7aac99625f","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:51:20.372Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/7e0f410179f755c7f1d64e80833584d3460c746dcb3ad83e944d3be87642747d.json\n---\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task usb4stream-bench: Author the wedge-safe stream-primitive first-light bench, its receipts bound, and the transport decision memo. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge,