.99.0.0/30 address, then readlink /sys/class/net/RAIL/device, then the parent xdomain, then the sibling service whose key attribute is stream, then the configfs group fn0's index attribute, then the device node /dev/tbstream suffixed with that index; require BOTH ends' fn0 configfs groups to exist before any open. (b) Exactly ONE open attempt per side, ever, blocking, under a 30 s alarm; any failure after that point: close whatever is open, kill the ssh child, write the receipt, exit — never reopen, never retry, never write configfs (read ring_size and throttling only). (c) Idempotence guard: if results/receipts/usb4stream.json already exists, exit 0 immediately WITHOUT touching any device — this is what makes harness retries storm-free by construction. (d) Skip preconditions, checked in this order BEFORE any device access, each producing receipt status pass with data.outcome 'skipped:REASON' and exit 0: (i) the pair serve is up — the API answers on the coordinator, or podman reports the serving container running on either node (check the worker over the control wire) — outcome 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable': the stream device shares cable A with the serving rails and a wedge would take the campaign's headline deliverable down, so this bench runs ONLY on an idle cable; (ii) ping -c1 -W2 to the rail peer fails — outcome 'skipped:rail-peer-unreachable'; (iii) either end's fn0 configfs group is missing — outcome 'skipped:configfs-group-missing'. Record data.serve_up true or false in EVERY receipt including skips. (e) Fixed schedule, no adaptivity, no retries: 50 iterations of 4 KiB ping-pong warmup (discarded); RTT at 64, 4096, 16384, 65536 bytes times 500 iterations with p50 and p99 per size; the allreduce-shaped simultaneous exchange at 8192, 16384, 65536 bytes times 500 (both sides write N bytes then read N bytes — ring 1024 times 4 KiB frames buffers this safely); throughput 256 MiB each direction; under 90 s wall total, whole run under a global timeout. (f) The receipt at results/receipts/usb4stream.json: one JSON object, step 'usb4stream', status ALWAYS 'pass' — this bench is evidence-gathering, not a campaign claim, so a mid-run abort is typed as data.outcome 'aborted:PHASE:ERRNO' rather than a fail status that would redden every later gate run; data carries outcome, per-size rtt and exchange p50/p99 fields, throughput both directions, ring_size and throttling as read from configfs, resolved device paths on both ends, open_count (assert exactly 1 per side), serve_up, and loop 'python' for honesty about syscall-loop overhead. (2) scripts/receipts-verify.py: add a 'usb4stream' entry to the BOUNDS table — outcome 'ok' requires open_count 1 and all schedule fields present; 'skipped:' and 'aborted:' outcomes require their reason text and pass. (3) docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md — the decision memo: why the collective-library net-plugin route is REJECTED for the latency goal (it sits under the library's proxy and protocol stack, HopID scarcity shared with the network paths forces a multiplexer over one or two long-lived streams, and comm teardown on every serve restart is exactly the open/close pattern the wedge hazard forbids; 3-5 attended days to a fragile prototype, 2-4 attended weeks to overnight-trustworthy); why the real path is a 2-4 attended-day port of the reference doorbell-plus-progress-thread allreduce (the 105 microsecond reference bar) from verbs onto the stream device's read and write, with the receive path run by the progress thread; the morning trigger criteria (banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix showing allreduce-dominated decode); the note that after a healthy night the first real run happens attended in the morning AFTER the pair is torn down (the serve-up skip is deliberate); and a drafted-not-filed issue body for the port. (4) tests/test_usb4stream_bench.py: py-compile both edited python files, assert the no-hardcoded-device-node invariant (no digit after tbstream in the bench source), assert the idempotence guard and the serve-up skip are present, and exercise the receipts checker's three outcome branches with synthetic receipt dicts. Boundaries: touch only bench/usb4stream-bench.py, docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md, scripts/receipts-verify.py, and tests/.\",\"id\":\"usb4stream-bench\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/dotfiles-observed.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\",\"bench/run-matrix.sh\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:75b32ae929f161f972eb9544f33d653ee19a939a595012f6c112e3c4e69bb00e\",\"title\":\"Author the wedge-safe stream-primitive first-light bench, its receipts bound, and the transport decision memo\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"0a89657f40b8654fed9a050b77458f46f0e5c559\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-ddeb5a9a4133/usb4stream-bench\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"bench/usb4stream-bench.py\",\"docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md\",\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/usb4stream-bench-75b32ae929f161f9\",\"taskId\":\"usb4stream-bench\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ddeb5a9a4133/usb4stream-bench\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[{\"author\":\"uid:1000\",\"body\":\"OVERSEER STANDING NOTE (all tasks — harness limitation, tally#622 family): the spec-build driver fails any lane whose squash merge stages ZERO change against the witnessed base (\\\"squash merge staged no change against the witnessed base\\\", exit 1), even when your no-change conclusion is technically correct. If you verify your deliverables are already fully present and acceptance passes, you must STILL land one small non-empty commit on your assigned branch, strictly inside your task's ownership paths: a short RECONCILE-<taskId>-2026-08-30.md note recording HEAD at verification and the acceptance evidence. Never conclude \\\"no commit needed\\\"; never use --allow-empty (squash still stages nothing). This applies especially to checkpoint re-runs whose outputs match the previously committed state byte-for-byte.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"id\":2,\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-30T03:50:41.902Z\",\"url\":\"local://campaign/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering/2\"}],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[2],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":0,\"recheckedCursor\":2,\"registrationId\":\"01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
