{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYGKjxvGzuGv3qLVXrCw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SgKQPtvkd8eP11wMHAWhX1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git add bench/usb4stream-bench.py docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md scripts/receipts-verify.py tests/test_usb4stream_bench.py && git commit -q -F - <<'MSG' && git status --porcelain && echo \"CLEAN\" && git log --oneline -1\nusb4stream-bench: Wedge-safe stream-primitive first light, its receipts bound, and the transport memo\n\nbench/usb4stream-bench.py — one file, three roles (coordinator default, peer\nover the control wire, read-only probe). Every mechanic exists because a\nfirst open enables router paths and a last close disables them: cycling that\nagainst a mismatched peer corrupts hop tables on cable A, which rail 0 and\nthe serving pair share, and that hazard darkened rail 0 once already.\n\n  * No numbered device literal anywhere. Resolution runs on EACH node: the\n    netdev holding the 10.99.0.0/30 -> readlink its device -> parent xdomain\n    -> sibling service with key=stream -> that service's fn0 configfs group\n    -> its index -> the device node. Verified read-only on the coordinator\n    today: thunderbolt0 -> xdomain 1-2 -> service 1-2.1 (key=stream) ->\n    /sys/kernel/config/thunderbolt/stream/1-2.1/fn0 (index=0, ring_size=1024,\n    throttling=2048) — a different index than the one recorded on 08-30,\n    which is exactly why nothing may be hardcoded. Both ends' fn0 groups are\n    required before any open.\n  * Exactly one open per side, ever, blocking, under a 30 s alarm; a second\n    call raises rather than retries. Any failure after that: close, kill the\n    ssh child, write the receipt, exit. Never reopen, never write configfs.\n  * Idempotence guard first of all — an existing receipt means exit 0 with no\n    device touched, so harness retries are storm-free by construction.\n  * Three skip preconditions in order, before any device access: a serve on\n    the shared cable (skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable — the expected outcome\n    after a healthy night), rail peer unreachable, either fn0 group missing.\n    data.serve_up is recorded in every receipt including skips.\n  * Fixed schedule, no adaptivity: 50 x 4 KiB warmup discarded; RTT at\n    64/4096/16384/65536 x 500 with p50/p99; the allreduce-shaped simultaneous\n    exchange at 8192/16384/65536 x 500; 256 MiB each direction; under a\n    global alarm.\n  * status is ALWAYS pass — this is evidence, not a claim, so a mid-run abort\n    types as data.outcome aborted:PHASE:ERRNO instead of reddening every\n    later gate run. loop: \"python\" is stated for syscall-loop honesty.\n\nscripts/receipts-verify.py — a usb4stream bound: ok requires open_count 1 per\nside plus the whole schedule (both RTT and exchange sizes with p50/p99, both\nthroughput directions, ring_size/throttling, resolved paths on both ends);\nskipped: and aborted: pass but must carry their reason text.\n\ndocs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md — the memo the morning reads instead of\nre-deliberating: the net-plugin route rejected for the latency goal (proxy\nstack, HopID scarcity forcing a multiplexer, comm teardown = the wedge\npattern; 3-5 attended days to a fragile prototype, 2-4 attended weeks to\novernight-trustworthy), the 2-4 attended-day doorbell-allreduce port as the\nreal path against the 105 us bar, the trigger criteria (exchange p50 at\n8-16 KiB <= ~40 us AND allreduce-dominated decode), why the serve-up skip is\ndeliberate and the first real run is attended after teardown, and a\ndrafted-not-filed issue body for the port.\n\ntests/test_usb4stream_bench.py — 24 tests: both files compile, no digit after\nthe device word in the bench source, the idempotence guard and the three\ntyped skips (in precondition order), one-open-per-side enforced, no configfs\nwrite, always-pass receipts, abort typing, and the checker's ok / skipped: /\naborted: branches against synthetic receipts.\nMSG","description":"Commit the lane's work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":647,"cache_read_input_tokens":120630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":647},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dad2f56-3033-4a9b-8df9-7c3428d04797","uuid":"ae4a9b9f-d6ee-4103-b52f-8b543f9f0b2d","timestamp":"2026-08-30T04:00:40.851Z","request_id":"req_011CeYGKj7pJ1txz1rY7e1yB"}
