{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYGMSNJmxqZnb58Y5ffe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Committed as `ac7d2be` on `tally-work/flashnext-ddeb5a9a4133/usb4stream-bench`; `git status --porcelain` prints nothing.\n\n**Acceptance** (`usb4stream-bench-sound`) passes: both Python files compile, the bench is configfs-driven with no numbered device literal, the serve-up skip is present, the memo is non-empty, and all 24 tests pass. The full suite (91 tests across all 7 modules) also passes, so the new `usb4stream` bound didn't disturb `test_repo_invariants`' clean `receipts-verify` run.\n\n**What landed** (all four paths inside the write boundary):\n\n- `bench/usb4stream-bench.py` — coordinator/peer/probe in one file; the peer is launched by streaming this file over the control wire (`ssh … python3 -`), never copied. One open per side ever (a second call raises), 30 s open alarm plus a global alarm, idempotence guard before anything, the three typed skips in the specified order with `data.serve_up` on every receipt, the fixed 4-phase schedule, and `status: \"pass\"` always with aborts typed as `aborted:PHASE:ERRNO`.\n- `scripts/receipts-verify.py` — a `usb4stream` BOUNDS entry: `ok` demands `open_count` 1 per side and the whole schedule; `skipped:`/`aborted:` pass but must carry reason text.\n- `docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md` — plugin route rejected with costs, the doorbell-allreduce port as the real path, trigger criteria, the deliberate serve-up skip, and a drafted-not-filed issue body.\n- `tests/test_usb4stream_bench.py` — the invariants plus the checker's three branches on synthetic receipts.\n\nOne thing worth flagging for the morning operator: I exercised the resolution chain read-only on this coordinator (no device opened), and it resolves `thunderbolt0 → xdomain 1-2 → service 1-2.1 (key=stream) → /sys/kernel/config/thunderbolt/stream/1-2.1/fn0`, which reports `index=0`, `ring_size=1024`, `throttling=2048`. Two consequences: the real configfs layout has a `stream/` level that my initial candidate roots missed (fixed, with the observed path recorded in a comment and `FN_USB4_CONFIGFS_ROOT` as an override), and the index here is **0**, not the 2 recorded in `docs/DECISIONS-2026-08-30.md` §5.2 — indices are not stable across re-enumeration. The memo now says to read `data.device` out of the receipt rather than any remembered number; the dynamic-resolution requirement is unaffected and, if anything, better justified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1718,"cache_read_input_tokens":121277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1718},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dad2f56-3033-4a9b-8df9-7c3428d04797","uuid":"4efe57b8-45d3-4a20-ac62-5e6c5155409b","timestamp":"2026-08-30T04:00:55.822Z","request_id":"req_011CeYGMRTzBwQ59yvEodkP1"}
